{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pnrcke3g7dw64az53aqa5cpga2ddtgjwqvr5uco5yrtpreqnavcq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe library turned out to be genuinely small — I verified this rather than assumed it. `c_src/` contains exactly three files (`CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h`, `src/lib.c`, 42 lines of code total), and `nm -D` on the built C `.so` exports exactly **one** public symbol:\n\n```\nT colourblind\n```\n\nThe other `nm` entries (`_ITM_*`, `__cxa_finalize`, `__gmon_start__`) are weak toolchain artifacts, not library API. The three transform helpers (`Protanopia`/`Deuteranopia`/`Tritanopia`) are `static`, so they are correctly *not* exported. No namespace-renaming macros exist in the header. Given the size, I did the work directly — delegating would have been pure overhead.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n```\nC exports   (1): colourblind\nRust exports(1): colourblind\n>>> SYMBOL DIFF EMPTY <<<\n```\n\n## The interesting part: byte-identical output\n\nThe naive translation compiled and was correct for all finite inputs, but my differential harness (which `dlopen`s both `.so`s and compares raw **bit patterns**) found 449 mismatches — all in **NaN sign propagation**.\n\nRoot cause: x86's `ADDSS`/`SUBSS`/`MULSS` return the *destination* operand when both operands are NaN. So which NaN survives depends on the operand order the compiler picked. LLVM canonicalizes commutative operands differently from GCC, and rewrites `x - k*y` into an add of a negated constant — flipping some NaN sign bits.\n\nTwo findings that shaped the fix:\n- This is *not* a stable property of the C source: GCC `-O0` and `-O1`/`-O2`/`-O3` disagree with **each other** on these NaN signs. The reference `CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, and I confirmed its output matches `-O0` exactly — so `-O0` is the authoritative target.\n- `_mm_*_ss` intrinsics **don't** work: I checked the disassembly and LLVM folds them straight back into scalar `fadd`/`fmul` and re-canonicalizes. The mismatch count stayed at exactly 449.\n\nThe fix transcribes GCC's operand order from `gcc -S -O0` output into a small `sse` module using inline `asm!`, which is opaque to those rewrites. Two distinct patterns emerged from the assembly — `add(t3, add(t1,t2))` for added third terms, `sub(add(t2,t1), t3)` for subtracted ones — encoded per-line with a comment showing the shape.\n\nVerification: **1,291,888 checks, 0 mismatches — BYTE-IDENTICAL**, covering a 65³ sweep of the unit cube × 3 impairments, 26 hostile special values (±0, denormals, `FLT_MIN`/`MAX`, ±inf, ±NaN, 2²⁴ boundaries) cubed, out-of-range impairment values, all 4 aliasing-pointer combinations, and 400k random raw-bit-pattern fuzz cases.\n\n## Fidelity notes\n\nBehaviors deliberately preserved rather than \"fixed\":\n- **Aliasing semantics** — the C reads all three components into locals *before* storing, then writes Red/Green/Blue in order. Observable when a caller passes the same pointer twice, so I used raw pointer reads/writes in that exact order instead of a safe by-value abstraction. Explicitly covered by the aliasing tests.\n- **No `default` arm** — the C `switch` silently ignores impairment values outside `{0,1,2}` (unsigned compare, so \"negative\" values too). Reproduced as a no-op `_ => {}`.\n- **No NULL checks** — the C dereferences unconditionally; I added none.\n- Tritanopia's paired constants differ in their decimal literals (`0.12739886310880` vs `0.12739886341072`) but round to the same `f32` — GCC shares one `.LC12` for both, which independently confirms my literals are transcribed correctly.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (mtimes still at the original checkout time, before my first command), and my scratch build/verification directory has been cleaned up. Final deliverable is `translation/Cargo.toml` (with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `translation/src/lib.rs`; clean `cargo build --release` from scratch is warning-free."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":71533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":282,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32810b32-b6d0-4e48-8b8f-42ef900d5faf","uuid":"8f148f6d-395c-4ce5-a9bb-376d54b908fd","timestamp":"2026-08-26T20:07:28.723Z"}
